            # of every tail part. `.` chains are left-deep, so the accumulator is
            # the LEFTMOST leaf; appending tail parts via strada_concat_inplace is
            # amortized O(appended bytes), vs the multi-part path's fresh
            # exactly-sized copy of the WHOLE accumulator each time — which makes
            # `$s = $s . ...` in a loop O(n^2) (the bench_utf8 concat hot spot).
            # Mirrors the `.=` fast path; safe under concat_inplace's COW rule.
